==Enemy==
This enemy works very similarly to [[Idi:Re]]. A rusher with the high speed and knockback count typical of Dark enemies, Crocodylidae Kurocroc attacks by running up to cats and biting down on them from 300 range with an added 150 piercing range, then backing up and standing in place for a moment, during which time Kurocroc will get to retaliate immediately if knocked back. Furthermore, they are immune to both freeze and slow, and will weaken anything hit by 50% with roughly 75% uptime. Their fairly long backswing makes them relatively easy to keep stalled until support arrives.

==Strategy==
Because of Crocodylidae Kurocroc's high damage and reach, you should consider using disposable units to chip at them between attack cycles, or have fast units trick Kurocroc into attacking early and missing after knocking them back, since their [[Omni Strike]]s allow them to reach deeper into backline units that would otherwise outrange them–such as [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Awakened Urs]]. Their attack rate is not the fastest, so rushers and quick attackers like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] can land devastating hits on them. Do '''NOT''' utilize [[:Category:Cats with Knockback ability|cats with the Knockback ability]], since they will reset Kurocroc's attack cycle. [[:Category:Cats with Weaken Immunity|Weaken-Immune cats]] such as the aforementioned Talented Heavy Assault C.A.T. are especially useful against this enemy, as Kurocroc's [[Weaken]] has a 75% uptime. Furthermore, their lack of [[Immune to Waves|Wave]]/[[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]] means that units such as [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] are also capable of sniping them from a distance. [[Adventurer Kanna (Uber Rare Cat)|Fabled Adventurer Girl Kanna]] in particular shreds this enemy; with [[Massive Damage]] against Dark and Behemoth Slayer amplifying her damage to 10x, she can use frontline peons as stepping stones to cripple Kurocroc from a distance with her [[Long Distance]] and [[Surge Attacks]].

Kurocroc becomes a far greater issue when paired with other enemies to defend them. With Kurocroc's help, other attackers will begin pushing far more efficiently into your backlines. Due to their many knockbacks, unreasonably high health and their ability to Weaken retaliations from anything non-immune they hit, Kurocroc will typically be the last thing standing. Expect them to be a persistent nuisance throughout a stage's duration, up until all other threats have been neutralized. Because of this, it is advised to focus on keeping them at bay while addressing more pressing matters, then strike when the time is right. In Behemoth‑centric stages, [[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]] and [[Ancient Egg: N103 (Rare Cat)|Gas Mask Cat]] will become invaluable, as they can typically hold out until their cooldowns refresh.

Overall, while this enemy may not be threatening on their own, their support abilities make them an overwhelming presence. Despite their mediocre pushing power when alone, they cannot be left unchecked; left to their own devices, they will swiftly chew through your defenses and allow increasingly more threatening enemy units into your backlines.

